{"slug": "bbq-beef-ribs", "nyt_id": 1014177, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014177-bbq-beef-ribs", "name": "BBQ Beef Ribs", "author": "Steven Raichlen", "description": "Just before being served, these ribs are grilled, imparting a crisp, charred crust and an inviting whiff of wood smoke. Steven Raichlen", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 240, "raw": {"total": "PT4H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Four 1-pound beef short ribs", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "four 1-pound beef short ribs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons vegetable oil, plus more for grill grate", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vegetable oil", "preparation": "plus more for grill grate", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 medium onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 carrots, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "carrots", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "5 cloves garlic, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "5 stalks lemon grass, trimmed and cut into 2-inch pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": "stalk", "item": "lemon grass", "preparation": "trimmed and cut into 2-inch pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 two-inch piece ginger, cut into ¼-inch slices", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "two-inch piece ginger", "preparation": "cut into ¼-inch slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 cup soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup dark brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "dark brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "¼ cup rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¾ cup ketchup", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "ketchup", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ cup dark brown sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "dark brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "½ cup rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "2 tablespoons mirin", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "mirin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "2 teaspoons soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "3 cloves garlic, peeled and lightly crushed with side of knife", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled and lightly crushed with side of knife", "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "3 ¼-inch slices fresh ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 3.25, "unit": null, "item": "inch slices fresh ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "For the ribs: Heat the oven to 325 degrees. Season the ribs all over with salt. In a large Dutch oven or other heavy pot, heat 2 tablespoons oil over medium-high heat. Add the ribs and brown on all sides, turning with tongs, 5 minutes a side. Transfer to a platter and pour off all but 2 tablespoons fat."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add the onion, carrots, garlic, lemon grass and ginger to the pot. Cook over high heat until lightly browned, 3 minutes. Stir in the soy sauce, brown sugar, rice vinegar and 3 cups water, and bring to a boil. Return the ribs to the pot, immersing them in the liquid. Tightly cover and bake, turning the ribs once or twice until very tender, about 3 ½ hours. Let the ribs cool in the liquid, then drain well. (Ribs can be refrigerated for up to 24 hours.)"}, {"position": 3, "text": "For the glaze: In a heavy saucepan, combine all the glaze ingredients and simmer over medium heat until thick, about 10 minutes. Strain."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Prepare a grill for direct grilling over high heat. Brush and oil the grate. Cook the ribs until dark brown all over, 3 to 5 minutes a side, basting with the glaze. Serve with the remaining glaze drizzled on top or passed separately in a bowl."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 1650.0, "protein_g": 72.8, "carbohydrates_g": 67.9, "fat_g": 171.9, "saturated_fat_g": 72.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.5, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 344.7, "sodium_mg": 4312.2, "fiber_g": 2.2, "sugar_g": 47.8, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["dark-brown-sugar", "short-rib", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/22/dining/Beef-Ribs/Beef-Ribs-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/22/dining/Beef-Ribs/Beef-Ribs-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 402}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-06-29", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:11:44Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bbq-beef-tongue", "nyt_id": 1013095, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013095-bbq-beef-tongue", "name": "BBQ Beef Tongue", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "Barbecue beef tongue, a bold, richly succulent dish that suited the unseasonal weather. The recipe is somewhat surprising. I expected the tongue to be slow-cooked over applewood or hickory, but the barbecue is contributed by a mere couple of tablespoons of sauce added to the braising liquid. Once the tongue is done — and it calls for quite an investment in unattended time — it is delicious. Florence Fabricant", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 300, "raw": {"total": "PT5H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 beef tongue, 2 to 3 pounds, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "beef tongue", "preparation": "2 to 3 pounds, rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ carrot, diced", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": null, "item": "carrot", "preparation": "diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 celery stalk, diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "celery stalk", "preparation": "diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 medium onion, diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 thyme sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "thyme sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup flat-leaf parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "flat-leaf parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon black peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "black peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 tablespoons Chinese or Thai barbecue sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chinese or thai barbecue sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 quart veal or beef stock", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "quart", "item": "veal or beef stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 quarts chicken stock", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "quart", "item": "chicken stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 ½ cups arugula or baby spinach", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "arugula or baby spinach", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 tablespoon red wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "red wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 tablespoon extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 325 degrees. In a deep ovenproof casserole, 5 to 6 quarts, place the tongue, carrot, celery, onion, thyme, parsley, peppercorns, barbecue sauce, veal stock and just enough chicken stock to cover tongue. Bring to a boil, stir, cover and place in the oven. Check liquid from time to time, adding more chicken stock as needed. When tongue is very tender, about 3 hours, remove it from pot to cool. Let uncovered pot cool about an hour."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Strain cooking liquid into a 4-quart saucepan, bring to a boil and reduce to 3 cups, about 45 minutes. Meanwhile, peel skin from tongue, wrap tongue in plastic and refrigerate at least 2 hours or overnight. (Reduced cooking liquid can also be refrigerated.)"}, {"position": 3, "text": "Slice tongue ½-inch thick. Arrange slices, slightly overlapping, in a large skillet. Pour reduced sauce over, bring to a simmer and cook about 30 minutes, until syrupy. Toss greens with vinegar and oil. Transfer tongue to a serving platter, spoon sauce over tongue and serve with greens alongside."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 539.8333333333334, "protein_g": 40.3, "carbohydrates_g": 26.4, "fat_g": 36.9, "saturated_fat_g": 14.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.7, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 174.0, "sodium_mg": 981.0, "fiber_g": 1.3, "sugar_g": 9.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["beef", "project"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/01/dining/bbq-beef-tongue/bbq-beef-tongue-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/01/dining/bbq-beef-tongue/bbq-beef-tongue-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 33}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-03-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:42:09Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
